.TH C99TERM 1 C99Term\-VERSION
.SH NAME
C99Term \- C99 terminal (fork of st with an Alacritty config)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c99term
.RB [ \-aiv ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR font ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR geometry ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR iofile ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR line ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR windowid ]
.RB [ \-\-config\-file
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-option
.IR toml ]
.RB [ \-\-working\-directory
.IR dir ]
.RB [[ \-e ]
.IR command
.RI [ arguments ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B c99term
is a C99 fork of suckless
.BR st (1).
It reads an Alacritty config (TOML or YAML) and adds scrollback, transparency
and Alacritty-like clipboard and keyboard behaviour. The program is
.B C99Term ;
the binary is
.BR c99term .
.I make install
also links it as
.I st
so existing launchers keep working.
.PP
On first run, if
.I ~/.config/c99term
does not exist, C99Term creates it and copies the first Alacritty config it
finds. The original is left in place. TERM defaults to
.BR xterm\-256color .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
disable alternate screens in the terminal.
.TP
.BI \-c " class"
defines the window class (default $TERM).
.TP
.BI \-f " font"
defines the font to use. Overridden by the config unless this flag is set.
.TP
.BI \-g " geometry"
defines the X11 geometry string.
The form is [=][<cols>{xX}<rows>][{+-}<xoffset>{+-}<yoffset>]. See
.BR XParseGeometry (3).
.TP
.B \-i
fix the position given with the \-g option.
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
defines the window instance name (default $TERM).
.TP
.BI \-o " iofile"
writes all I/O to
.I iofile.
A value of "\-" means standard output. This is the I/O file, not a config
option. Use \-\-option for config overrides.
.TP
.BI \-T " title"
defines the window title (default 'C99Term').
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
defines the window title (default 'C99Term').
.TP
.BI \-w " windowid"
embeds C99Term within the window identified by
.I windowid.
.TP
.BI \-l " line"
use a tty
.I line
instead of a pseudo terminal. Remaining arguments are
.BR stty (1)
flags. See
.BR stty (1).
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file " file"
load this Alacritty or C99Term config instead of the default search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-option " toml"
override a config key, for example
.BR window.opacity=0.8 .
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-working\-directory " dir"
chdir here before starting the shell.
.TP
.BI \-e " command " [ " arguments " "... ]"
execute
.I command
instead of the shell. Must be the last option.
.SH SHORTCUTS
Alacritty's Linux defaults, unless the config overrides them:
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-c
Copy the selection to CLIPBOARD.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Shift\-v
Paste from CLIPBOARD.
.TP
.B Shift\-Insert
Paste from PRIMARY.
.TP
.B Shift\-Page Up / Page Down
Scroll a page.
.TP
.B Shift\-Home / End
Scroll to the top or bottom of the history.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-= / Ctrl\-\- / Ctrl\-0
Zoom in, out, or reset.
.PP
The wheel scrolls history. On the alternate screen (vim, less) it moves the
cursor unless Shift is held. Typing or pasting jumps back to the bottom.
Dragging a selection to the top or bottom edge scrolls and extends the
highlight.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
Colours, font and keys come from the Alacritty config. Compile-time defaults
live in
.I src/config.def.h.
.SH AUTHORS
See the LICENSE file. C99Term is a fork of suckless st; the original authors
are listed there.
.SH LICENSE
MIT/X. See the LICENSE file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stty (1),
.BR alacritty (1)
.SH BUGS
GPU drawing, Wayland, Vi mode, search and hints are not implemented.
